Third-party components
----------------------

P2S Local calls, links and ships third-party software under their own licences.
The authoritative, per-version register (with evidence links) is
configs/licenses.yaml; the weights register is configs/models.lock.

  * Called as subprocesses, not bundled: ffmpeg (this build is GPL-2.0-or-later),
    MuseScore Studio (GPL-3.0), FluidSynth (LGPL-2.1-or-later, dev only).
  * Linked libraries include LGPL-3.0 (Verovio, cairosvg), LGPL-2.1-or-later
    (soxr), Apache-2.0 (partitura, lightning, transformers, uvicorn,
    python-multipart), MIT (pydantic, PyYAML, pretty_midi, fastapi, …) and
    BSD-3-Clause (numpy, scipy, pandas, music21, httpx, soundfile, pypdf, …).
  * Benchmark oracles used locally and never shipped: VeroSim, musicdiff
    (no published licence — results cite them without redistribution).

Model weights and datasets
--------------------------

No model weights and no audio or score datasets are distributed in this
repository; they are downloaded separately under their own terms.
Relevant constraints for v1:

  * Transkun v2 and Beat This! — MIT code and weights.
  * M2ST (TimFelixBeyer/MIDI2ScoreTransformer) — code and weights state no
    licence. Internal, noncommercial evaluation only.
  * Aria-AMT — Apache-2.0 code, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 weights.
  * PM2S — MIT code, CC BY 4.0 weights (Zendo record 10520196), benchmark only.
  * MAESTRO and ASAP — CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (audio and scores).
  * MuseScore General / MS Basic soundfont — MIT.

Because several of these are noncommercial (and one has no stated licence), the
project as a whole is noncommercial. Relicensing for commercial use requires
replacing or re-clearing every engine and dataset above first.
